@section(Debugging in the document)

The debugger block is @@visual_debug (see code/06-visual-debug.idoc). @@vdebug and @@visualdebug are two more spellings of it:

@vdebug(language=systemverilog, src=blink.sv, h=200px)

@visualdebug(language=systemverilog, src=blink.sv, h=200px)

@section(Where documents live)

A workspace is where your files are. There are four kinds:

@dl
server: your own space on the IDoc server, reachable from any computer you sign in on.
folder: a folder on this computer, opened through the browser.
drive: Google Drive.
none: open one file, edit it and save it back.
@end

On the server your own folder is private. A colleague can be given read or edit access to one document; it stays where it is and they open it under shares. Every save compares what the tab last read with what is on disk, so a stale tab cannot overwrite someone else's change. Version history keeps snapshots and deleted files go to a trash you can restore from.

@section(Working together)

Live co-editing is off until someone turns it on. A lobby keeps the server's copy as the document, shows who is in it with cursor colours, and keeps comments attached to the words they are about.

@box(w=100%, style=offline)
Server workspaces, sharing and live co-editing need the IDoc server.
@end

@section(File types)

@dl
.idoc: a document.
.style: a stylesheet, applied with @@style(Name).
.course: a course file, read by Docent.
.profile: who you are, read by @@getvar.
.dict: an equation library, read by @@eq.
.ans: a generated answer key for scanned papers.
.bib: BibTeX references.
.bml .bct .cmesh .bdem: compressed map, table, mesh and terrain blocks.
@end

Exports: PDF, PowerPoint with or without narration, EPUB, Braille STL, QTI, answer keys and grades.csv. Imports: Word, PDF, Markdown, HTML, plain text, LaTeX, GIFT, Aiken, QTI, Common Cartridge and Moodle backups.
